<section class="section" id="faq">

    <div class="section-heading">

        <span class="section-number">
            24 — FAQ
        </span>

        <h2>
            Mr. Mime FAQ
        </h2>

    </div>


    <details>

        <summary>
            What type is Mr. Mime?
        </summary>

        <p>

            Kanto Mr. Mime is a Psychic/Fairy-type Pokémon.

        </p>

    </details>


    <details>

        <summary>
            What is Mr. Mime weak to?
        </summary>

        <p>

            Mr. Mime is vulnerable to Ghost, Poison and
            Steel-type attacks.

        </p>

    </details>


    <details>

        <summary>
            Is Shiny Mr. Mime available?
        </summary>

        <p>

            Yes. Shiny Mr. Mime is available through eligible
            Pokémon GO encounters.

        </p>

    </details>


    <details>

        <summary>
            Is Shadow Mr. Mime available?
        </summary>

        <p>

            Shadow availability can depend on current Team GO
            Rocket rotations and events. Check current game
            data before treating it as an active encounter.

        </p>

    </details>


    <details>

        <summary>
            What is a 100% Mr. Mime?
        </summary>

        <p>

            A 100% Mr. Mime has 15 Attack, 15 Defense and
            15 HP IVs.

        </p>

    </details>


    <details>

        <summary>
            What is Lucky Mr. Mime?
        </summary>

        <p>

            Lucky Mr. Mime is a special Pokémon obtained
            through trading and has the Lucky status.

        </p>

    </details>


    <details>

        <summary>
            Is XXL Mr. Mime stronger?
        </summary>

        <p>

            No. XXL is a size designation and does not
            automatically mean better IVs or battle performance.

        </p>

    </details>


    <details>

        <summary>
            Is XXS Mr. Mime rare?
        </summary>

        <p>

            XXS specimens can be desirable to collectors because
            they represent an unusually small size category.

        </p>

    </details>


    <details>

        <summary>
            Does Mr. Mime evolve?
        </summary>

        <p>

            Mr. Mime is associated with Mime Jr. in its
            evolutionary family. Evolution requirements should
            be checked against the current Pokémon GO mechanics.

        </p>

    </details>


    <details>

        <summary>
            Is Mr. Mime good for raids?
        </summary>

        <p>

            Mr. Mime is generally more valuable as a collectible
            or specialty Pokémon than as a top-tier raid attacker.

        </p>

    </details>


    <details>

        <summary>
            Is Mr. Mime good in PvP?
        </summary>

        <p>

            Mr. Mime is a niche PvP option. Its usefulness
            depends heavily on the current league, moveset and
            metagame.

        </p>

    </details>


    <details>

        <summary>
            What is the difference between Mr. Mime and Galarian Mr. Mime?
        </summary>

        <p>

            Galarian Mr. Mime is a distinct regional form with
            different typing and gameplay characteristics.
            It should be treated separately from Kanto Mr. Mime
            in a Pokémon GO database.

        </p>

    </details>


</section>



